{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Separating "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" can cause unexpected runtime issues when the same query key is accidentally used with more than one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":". Wrapping them in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"infiniteQueryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":") co-locates the key and function, making queries safer and easier to reuse."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rule-details","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule Details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incorrect"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const query = useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n  // ...\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction useFooQuery(id) {\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction getFooOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const query = useQuery(getFooOptions(id))\n  // ...\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction getFooOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction useFooQuery(id) {\n  return useQuery({ ...getFooOptions(id), select: (data) => data.foo })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rule also enforces reusing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" from a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" result instead of typing it manually in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" methods or filters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incorrect"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" references for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.getQueryData(['todo', id])\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todo', id] })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" references for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.getQueryData(todoOptions(id).queryKey)\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: todoOptions(id).queryKey })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-not-to-use-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When Not To Use It"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you do not want to enforce the use of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" in your codebase, you will not need this rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"attributes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Recommended (strict)"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🔧 Fixable"}]}],"checked":false}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rule-details","text":"Rule Details","level":2},{"id":"when-not-to-use-it","text":"When Not To Use It","level":2},{"id":"attributes","text":"Attributes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSeparating `queryKey` and `queryFn` can cause unexpected runtime issues when the same query key is accidentally used with more than one `queryFn`. Wrapping them in `queryOptions` (or `infiniteQueryOptions`) co-locates the key and function, making queries safer and easier to reuse.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const query = useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction useFooQuery(id) {\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction getFooOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const query = useQuery(getFooOptions(id))\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction getFooOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction useFooQuery(id) {\n  return useQuery({ ...getFooOptions(id), select: (data) => data.foo })\n}\n```\n\nThe rule also enforces reusing `queryKey` from a `queryOptions` result instead of typing it manually in `QueryClient` methods or filters.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** `queryKey` references for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.getQueryData(['todo', id])\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todo', id] })\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** `queryKey` references for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.getQueryData(todoOptions(id).queryKey)\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: todoOptions(id).queryKey })\n}\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you do not want to enforce the use of `queryOptions` in your codebase, you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended (strict)\n- [ ] 🔧 Fixable\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: prefer-query-options\ntitle: Prefer the use of queryOptions\n---\n\nSeparating `queryKey` and `queryFn` can cause unexpected runtime issues when the same query key is accidentally used with more than one `queryFn`. Wrapping them in `queryOptions` (or `infiniteQueryOptions`) co-locates the key and function, making queries safer and easier to reuse.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const query = useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction useFooQuery(id) {\n  return useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction getFooOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const query = useQuery(getFooOptions(id))\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction getFooOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['get', id],\n    queryFn: () => Api.get(`/foo/${id}`),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction useFooQuery(id) {\n  return useQuery({ ...getFooOptions(id), select: (data) => data.foo })\n}\n```\n\nThe rule also enforces reusing `queryKey` from a `queryOptions` result instead of typing it manually in `QueryClient` methods or filters.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** `queryKey` references for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.getQueryData(['todo', id])\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todo', id] })\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** `queryKey` references for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.getQueryData(todoOptions(id).queryKey)\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-options\": \"error\" */\n\nfunction todoOptions(id) {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id),\n  })\n}\n\nfunction Component({ id }) {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n  return queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: todoOptions(id).queryKey })\n}\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you do not want to enforce the use of `queryOptions` in your codebase, you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended (strict)\n- [ ] 🔧 Fixable\n"}
